+## 2026-08-13 — Capacity-cost routing: the routing cost is the static pipe tier (amends the 2026-08-10 routing ruling)
+
+- **User ruling (problem-solving session 2026-08-13, artifact
+  `_bmad-output/problem-solution-2026-08-13.md`):** path cost = **STATIC pipe
+  capacity** — each pipe's routing cost is its tier's integer `cost`
+  (data/pipe_tiers.json ladder **20/10/5** for narrow/standard/wide), NEVER
+  dynamic utilization. Intent = traffic engineering: **"flows prefer fat
+  pipes"**; congestion avoidance stays the PLAYER's job (QoS lanes + pipe
+  engineering) — that is the game. The 4-rule spine (ODN-9/ODN-10) is
+  untouched: static weights keep the table a pure function of the Topology
+  (rebuild-on-topology-change holds by construction), the ECMP pick stays the
+  pure hash, the table stays derived (not T1-serialized).
+- **Decision — the SPF is now a Dijkstra over integer pipe costs:**
+  - `routing_rebuild` computes `dist[*]` in cost units; the equal-cost
+    next-hop condition is the textbook SPF test `dist[v] + cost(pipe) ==
+    dist[u]` — **equal cost is an END-TO-END sum property**, so a TRUE tie
+    across different tiers still ECMPs (standard(10)+wide(5) ==
+    wide(5)+standard(10) = 15 → ECMP set of 2), while unequal costs pick the
+    fatter path as a UNIQUE next hop.
+  - Cheapest-first extraction is an array min-scan with insertion-order
+    (slot-order) tie-breaks — no map iteration, no floats, no rng (ODN-10).
+  - A mixed-tier bundle prices at its fattest member (min member cost —
+    consistent with the bundle rendering at its highest member tier), so an
+    upgrade visibly attracts flow.
+  - Cost ladder lives in `data/pipe_tiers.json` (ODN-5): validated `cost >=
+    1` at catalog load (a zero-cost edge would break the per-hop progress
+    guarantee) and REJECTED otherwise; retuning the ladder is a data change.
+  - **Player rule (one line, in the GDD):** "packets take the fattest route;
+    equal cost splits by hash." Readable from the map (tiers are visible).
+- **What this changes:** the 2026-08-10 ruling's cost semantics (hop-count
+  BFS → capacity-cost Dijkstra). What it does NOT change: ECMP hash,
+  bundling, rebuild trigger, derived-table rule, QoS orthogonality, draw
+  cost, transit math, LOG_VERSION (no new commands).
+- **Deferred (scope-guarded out of this job):** the assist/readability
+  package (draw-time flow preview, post-draw route glow, tie cues — Job B),
+  the forecast flow-shift prediction (Job C), per-class routing preferences
+  (full-game idea, not this ruling).
